<title>SINGAPORE: UOL signs shareholders agreement.</title>
<headline>UOL signs shareholders agreement.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>United Overseas Land Ltd (UOL) said on Friday it had entered an agreement on shareholding with two companies to regulate investments related to Novena Square, a commercial site in central Singapore.</p>
<p>It said in a statement the subscription and shareholders agreement was to oversee Novena Square Investments Pte Ltd (NSIPL) and Novena Square Development Pte Ltd (NSDPL).</p>
<p>UOL signed the agreements with a unit of United Overseas Bank Ltd, UOB Warehouse Pte Ltd, and a unit of Singapore Land Ltd, S.L. Properties Ltd.</p>
<p>UOL will hold 60 percent, and the other two companies 20 percent each in NSIPL and NSDPL, both of which were incorporated in June to develop a commercial site in central Singapore.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
